WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
[MUSIC]

00:00:13.266 --> 00:00:17.866
There are three critical communication
tools that every business leader needs to

00:00:17.866 --> 00:00:20.880
be thinking about as he or
she communicates.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.170
The first is to have structure
to what it is you say.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.720
Structure is absolutely critical.

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.755
A wonderful structure to think about is
the what, so what, now what structure.

00:00:31.755 --> 00:00:36.920
This structure helps you convey a point,
teach people things in some cases,

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.060
convince them.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:41.880
You first start with the what, that is the
main point you're trying to get across.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.830
Perhaps it's a new product
you're bringing to market.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.070
Perhaps it's a new process
you're trying to implement.

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:52.270
The so what explains why it's important,
not to you, the communicator, but

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:53.360
to the audience.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.178
What's the value for them?

00:00:55.178 --> 00:00:59.570
And then the now what is what
you want your audience to do.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.156
Having that structure helps
you formalize your thoughts,

00:01:03.156 --> 00:01:07.969
package up your information, and it helps
you as a communicator to be concise.

00:01:07.969 --> 00:01:14.112
[MUSIC]

00:01:14.112 --> 00:01:19.027
The next tool you need to have is to
have variety in your communication, and

00:01:19.027 --> 00:01:22.000
I mean variety in many different ways.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.980
First, you need to have
variation in your voice.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:28.949
What we know is monotone speakers
are boring and disengaging.

00:01:28.949 --> 00:01:33.551
So we need to have some variation
both in our rate and in our volume.

00:01:33.551 --> 00:01:38.005
Second, we need to have variation
in the evidence that we provide.

00:01:38.005 --> 00:01:42.078
Whenever you make a claim,
make an argument, you need to support it,

00:01:42.078 --> 00:01:46.180
many people, especially in
the business world, use data.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:50.020
Data are critical and very important,
and I encourage people to use data,

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:54.290
especially if it's contextualized,
if you give it context.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:58.660
But there are other ways of
supporting your claims, use stories.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:02.770
Use testimonials,
that's a third party voice, define terms.

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:07.425
Those are ways that you can also vary,
supporting your claims.

00:02:07.425 --> 00:02:13.514
[MUSIC]

00:02:13.514 --> 00:02:16.202
The final tool I think every effective

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:21.380
business communicator needs to
have is the ability to paraphrase.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:25.730
Paraphrasing is a tool that helps in so
many contexts.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:31.430
For example, if somebody is making
an argument or raising a question,

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:37.100
yet they're very unclear and it's not for
sure what it is they need, paraphrase.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.720
Say something like what I
think you're asking is, or

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.250
the point I hear you making is this.

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:46.150
That helps solidify for
them what it is they're saying and

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:49.490
it gives you a launching point for
your response.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:53.000
Similarly, if you're in a meeting and
somebody is raising objections or

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:57.450
behaving rudely, you can use a paraphrase
to say, I hear what you're saying.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:59.430
That's something you're
very passionate about.

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:04.790
What I'd like to do next is, so
the paraphrase is a polite way to move

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:10.745
from somebody else's communication to
where you need the communication to go.

00:03:10.745 --> 00:03:15.065
With these three tools,
being structured, having variation,

00:03:15.065 --> 00:03:19.495
both in your voice and in your evidence,
and using paraphrasing.

00:03:19.495 --> 00:03:24.162
You can be very effective in the many
different types of situations you find

00:03:24.162 --> 00:03:25.060
yourself in.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:31.466
[MUSIC]

